  "# Codegen co-scientist, iteration 10

WIP=1 after iteration 9 was to **time**, not to compile. Round 1 already
matches LLVM's scalar shape (one mul of n, eight constant adds). Round 2 is
unique-use madd. Remainder is Mersenne. The leftover named in 9 is harness
and fuel, not another isel pass. This iteration measures that leftover
without changing it.

## What was timed

Pair, Apple M4, same protocol as iteration 6:

- amu native leaf via `kexe-benchmark` (`kexe_fn8`, context v3, `fuel = 512`
  rewritten every call)
- LLVM: `rustc --edition 2021 -C opt-level=3 -C codegen-units=1` of
  `kernel_wide.rs`, kernel inlined into the timed loop
- n=200, 100k calls, 10k warmup
- 21 rotated samples (even runs amu first, odd LLVM first)
- Judge: min ns/call

Native override only: amu still pins `314f9be9`. Compile used
`:local/root` of the CSE commit (`f3c8103`, merge `c15026ff` on origin/main).
amu pin was not bumped. nbb `bin/amu compile` still ICEs on bigint 48271;
JVM `clojure -M:run compile` produced the artifact.

Dump: `/tmp/kernel-wide-time-260818/`.

## Encoding of the timed bytes

Extracted `kernel` is 576 B at offset 0 (iteration 6 after the pool: 612 B).

| insn | count |
|---|---:|
| MUL (Ra=31) | 1 |
| MADD | 8 |
| SMULH | 16 |

SMULH is the Mersenne remainder, not a first-round multiply. This is the
iteration-9 encoding, actually running.

## Oracle

Every sample, both arms, answered **5224842816**. Same value as iteration 4
and the one-shot LLVM probe in this session.

## Times

loadavg `{ 24.40 24.66 26.58 }` at start and end. This is not a quiet
machine. Medians are contention. Min is the judge and still not a seal.

| arm | min | median | p95 | max |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| amu native | 15.68 | 26.50 | 32.70 | 35.89 |
| LLVM rustc -O3 | 11.06 | 19.26 | 24.12 | 34.52 |

min ratio **1.42x**. median ratio 1.38x.

Iteration 6 on a quieter machine: amu 10.0 ns, **1.62x** LLVM (LLVM then
about 6.2 ns). This session's LLVM min is 11.06 ns — roughly 1.8x slower
host than that ranking. Scaling 10.0 ns by that host factor lands near
18 ns; this min is 15.68 ns. That is **not** evidence CSE closed the LLVM
gap. It is evidence the host was noisy and the encoding change did not
move the ranking enough to replace 1.62x.

Do not write 1.42x into `amu/docs/performance.md`. Do not bump amu.

## What this does not change

- Fuel-on-entry remains. `kexe-benchmark.c` stores `context.fuel = 512`
  before every invoke. LLVM has none.
- LLVM still inlines into the 100k loop. amu still calls a function
  pointer. Putting that loop in the artifact was refuted in iteration 5
  (5.6x worse).
- The call / all-vreg path is unchanged (iteration 8).
- Seal only via `kotoba-lang/perfgate`, this kernel, min quantile, 25
  rotated samples, on a machine whose LLVM min is in the same band as
  iteration 6.

## Next

The leaf encoding already matches. The remaining gap on this workload is
the published runner (call + fuel), not another isel pass. Do not land
fused-srem, extra MOV peepholes, FMA, PGO, a kototama optimizer, or a
timed `bench` export. Do not overwrite iterations 04–09. Do not claim
LLVM beaten."}]
